profiles

List browser profiles available for new task spaces.

await profiles()

listTaskSpaces

List Agent-owned and user-owned spaces available to reuse or claim.

await listTaskSpaces()

taskSpace

Reuse or create an Agent-owned task space; a name held by a user-owned space fails with EGO_TASK_SPACE_NAME_IN_USE. A new space starts with managed Page p1, and profileId applies only when creating it. Options: profileId: Browser profile id returned by profiles(); new spaces only.

await taskSpace(nameOrId, { profileId? })

claimTaskSpace

Claim a user-owned or inactive space after user approval and return TaskSpace.

await claimTaskSpace(spaceId)

takeOverTaskSpace

Resume an Agent-owned space after user approval and return TaskSpace.

await takeOverTaskSpace(spaceId)

TaskSpace.spaceId

Stable numeric identifier for this task space.

task.spaceId

TaskSpace.name

Human-readable task-space name.

task.name

TaskSpace.ownership

Ownership state captured when this TaskSpace was created.

task.ownership

TaskSpace.page

Create a lazy handle for an existing managed Page label; it neither creates a Page nor checks that the label exists.

task.page(label)

TaskSpace.userPage

Return the tab active at the claim/takeover boundary, when one was captured.

task.userPage()

TaskSpace.pages

List the managed Page handles in this space.

await task.pages()

TaskSpace.tabs

List managed Pages and unmanaged tabs in this space.

await task.tabs()

TaskSpace.newPage

Create and durably label a blank Page.

await task.newPage()

TaskSpace.adopt

Bring an unmanaged tab under the Page lifecycle. Options: as: Permanent Page label.

await task.adopt(unmanagedPage, { as? })

TaskSpace.release

Stop managing an unknown-origin Page without closing it.

await task.release(label)

TaskSpace.waitForControl

Wait for Agent control without taking it from the user. Options: interval: Polling interval in milliseconds. timeout: Maximum duration in milliseconds.

await task.waitForControl({ interval?, timeout? })

TaskSpace.handOff

Give control of this space to the user.

await task.handOff()

TaskSpace.finish

Finish the task and return a receipt with retained and closed managed Page labels; an empty list closes the space when no protected tabs remain. Options: keep: Required Page retention policy: "all" or an array of managed Page labels.

await task.finish({ keep })

TaskSpace.cdp

Send a Target or Browser domain CDP command. Options: timeout: Maximum duration in milliseconds.

await task.cdp(method, params?, { timeout? })

Page.label

Durable Page label used to restore the tab across rounds.

page.label

Page.spaceId

Numeric identifier of the Page's task space.

page.spaceId

Page.openedBy

Conservative origin attribution for this Page.

page.openedBy

Page.targetId

Internal browser target identifier for advanced Target-domain CDP only.

page.targetId

Page.goto

Navigate this Page in place. Timeout errors report whether the new document committed, plus its URL and readyState when available. Options: referer: HTTP Referer header for the navigation. timeout: Maximum duration in milliseconds. waitUntil (commit | domcontentloaded | load | networkidle): Completion state; defaults to load. networkidle requires 500ms without network activity.

await page.goto(url, { referer?, timeout?, waitUntil? })

Page.reload

Reload this Page and wait for the selected navigation state. Options: timeout: Maximum duration in milliseconds. waitUntil (commit | domcontentloaded | load | networkidle): Completion state; defaults to load. networkidle requires 500ms without network activity.

await page.reload({ timeout?, waitUntil? })

Page.snapshot

Return a semantic snapshot of the current viewport, full Page, or one snapshot-ref subtree with Page provenance. Options: scope (full_page | only_within_viewport | subtree): Snapshot scope; defaults to only_within_viewport, including visible iframe content returned by the browser. Use subtree with an iframe root ref to focus on that frame. root: Valid Page snapshot ref such as @21; required only when scope is subtree. Partial snapshots preserve existing node identities. includeActionMarks: Include action marks. includeStableLocator: Include stable locators.

await page.snapshot({ scope?, root?, includeActionMarks?, includeStableLocator? })

Page.screenshot

Capture this Page to a PNG file. Options: path: Absolute output path; missing parent directories are created. fullPage: Capture the full scrollable page. clip: CSS-pixel clipping rectangle. scale (css): Output scale mode; css uses CSS-pixel sizing and is the default. raw: Bypass device-pixel-ratio correction.

await page.screenshot({ path?, fullPage?, clip?, scale?, raw? })

Page.url

Read this Page's current URL.

await page.url()

Page.waitForURL

Wait for an exact URL, Playwright-style glob, RegExp, or synchronous predicate receiving a URL object. Options: timeout: Maximum duration in milliseconds.

await page.waitForURL(urlMatcher, { timeout? })

Page.waitForEvent

Wait for this Page's next "popup" or "download"; arm the promise before the triggering action. Options: timeout: Maximum duration in milliseconds.

await page.waitForEvent(event, { timeout? })

Download.page

